\title{A native stop moved to set levels at set profits, and switched to trailing at the last}
\description{
This is an adjustable stop, the Atlas's G8. The stop-limit is placed at \code{stop_price}, and each rule names a \code{gain}, the profit in points from \code{entry_price} that sets it off, and either a \code{stop_at_gain}, where to move the stop measured from \code{entry_price}, or a \code{trail_points}, which starts the stop trailing as a \code{TrailingStopOrder} does. A market that jumps past several gains applies them all in one modification, a stop is only ever moved in the position's favour, and a trailing rule must be the last. Set \code{transaction_type} to the side that opened the position, so a long position is protected by asking for \code{buy}.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
}
